+
+If no acceptable URL exists, MarufYT declines its replacement and leaves the host's
+streaming state untouched. This does not prohibit the original host from handling
+its own data. Hostname syntax validation is **not** a Google-only allowlist,
+DNS/ownership check, private-address block or proof that an HTTPS host is trustworthy.
+
+### Downstream inspection
+
+`HLSPlayback.mm:285–313`, `YTKACEHLSFilterManifest` / `YTKACEHLSParseString`, inspect
+manifest text to omit unsupported VP9 variants. They do **not** enforce URL policy
+on child playlists, segment URIs, HLS key/map URIs or native-player redirects.
+The native host/AVFoundation transport receives the selected manifest. Its later
+URL resolution, credentials, cookie behavior and redirects are **unverified**.
+
+`Tweak/Runtime/URLPolicy.mm:10–28` and SABR/DirectDownloader/DownloadCoordinator
+delegates do validate their own redirects. SABR also checks its protobuf redirect
+at `SABRDownloader.mm:1421`. These are separate paths: their tests cannot establish
+that native HLS children or redirects use the same delegate. **No downstream
+security fix or runtime pass is claimed.**
