+### A. Passive iPhone packet capture on a Mac
+
+Connect the unlocked phone by USB, trust the Mac and use compatible Xcode device
+support. Get its UDID locally from Xcode's Devices and Simulators window. Apple
+documents RVI capture of the device's full network stack; it is not per-app capture.
+[Apple packet-trace instructions](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/network/recording-a-packet-trace).
+
+```sh
+# Run on the capture Mac, not this Windows workspace. Replace the placeholder locally.
+DEVICE_UDID="REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_UDID"
+mkdir -p "$HOME/MarufYT-private-captures"
+chmod 700 "$HOME/MarufYT-private-captures"
+rvictl -s "$DEVICE_UDID"
+# Use the interface printed above; rvi0 is an example, not a guaranteed index.
+sudo tcpdump -i rvi0 -n -s 0 -w "$HOME/MarufYT-private-captures/Latest-N01.pcap"
+# Perform only N01, then Ctrl-C. Repeat with a separate name per case/build.
+rvictl -x "$DEVICE_UDID"
+```
+
+If `rvictl`/pairing is unavailable, mark capture blocked and use compatible Apple
+tools; do not infer device results from this document. No capture commands were run
+here. On Windows, a Wi-Fi proxy below cannot replace RVI's all-stack visibility.
+
+Analyze a local copy in Wireshark. These read-only `tshark` examples export limited
+metadata, not raw URLs/headers/bodies; verify available fields with your installed
+tool. The TLS SNI field and QUIC dissector are documented by
+[Wireshark TLS reference](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/dfref/t/tls.html) and
+[QUIC reference](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/dfref/q/quic.html).
+
+```sh
+tshark -r Latest-N01.pcap -Y 'dns.flags.response == 0 && dns.qry.name' -T fields -e frame.time_relative -e dns.qry.name
+tshark -r Latest-N01.pcap -Y 'tls.handshake.type == 1' -T fields -e frame.time_relative -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name
+tshark -r Latest-N01.pcap -Y 'quic || udp.port == 443' -T fields -e frame.time_relative -e ip.dst -e ipv6.dst -e udp.dstport
+tshark -r Latest-N01.pcap -Y 'http.request || http.response.code' -T fields -e frame.time_relative -e tcp.stream -e http.host -e http.request.method -e http.response.code
+tshark -r Latest-N01.pcap -Y 'websocket || http.response.code == 101' -T fields -e frame.time_relative -e tcp.stream
+```
+
+DNS caching/encrypted DNS can hide queries; ECH can hide the actual TLS hostname;
+QUIC/HTTP3 may evade TCP-only analysis. IP ownership, shared CDNs and SNI alone
+cannot identify a feature or its payload. WSS/HTTP2 extended CONNECT, HTTPS paths,
+status codes and redirects require decryptable traffic or other authorized
+instrumentation. No visible 101 or DNS query does not prove absence.
+
+### B. Optional selective Wi-Fi HTTPS inspection on Windows or Mac
+
+Use a locally installed mitmweb with its version/options recorded. On an isolated
+test Wi-Fi, bind the proxy to the PC's actual private LAN address and allow that
+port only from the test phone. Keep the web UI on loopback. Inspect optional-service
+TLS only at first; Google authentication remains pass-through. Regular mode and
+host-selection settings follow the official
+[proxy modes](https://docs.mitmproxy.org/stable/concepts/modes/) and
+[options](https://docs.mitmproxy.org/stable/concepts/options/) documentation.
+
+```powershell
+# Replace <PC_LAN_IP> locally; do not run with this literal placeholder.
+mitmweb --mode regular --listen-host <PC_LAN_IP> --listen-port 8080 --web-host 127.0.0.1 --web-port 8081 --set 'allow_hosts=^(sponsor\.ajay\.app|dearrow-thumb\.ajay\.app|raw\.githubusercontent\.com|api\.aisloplist\.com)(:443)?$'
+```
+
+On iPhone, select the test Wi-Fi's information page → Configure Proxy → Manual;
+enter that PC address/8080. Visit `http://mitm.it` in Safari and install only this
+test proxy's CA profile. Enable full trust under Settings → General → About →
+Certificate Trust Settings. UI labels may vary on the actual OS. These steps and
+the certificate/pinning limits are described in the official
+[mitmproxy certificate guide](https://docs.mitmproxy.org/stable/concepts/certificates/).
+Keep the proxy CA private key/configuration local and out of GitHub and reports.
+
+Keep normal upstream certificate validation enabled. Do not use trust-all options,
+patch pinning, alter Google security checks or modify the IPA. Do not save raw HAR,
+flow dumps or screenshots containing headers. Inspect locally and report only
+domain/path template, method/status, and sensitive-header **presence yes/no/unknown**.
+Proxy bypass/QUIC and certificate rejection mean partial coverage, not an app pass.
+For login/switching, turn the proxy off and retain passive capture only.
+
+### C. Redirect chains, HLS children and controlled fallback
+
+For decryptable flows, inspect each 3xx response's Location locally; record only
+scheme, destination domain and redacted path template. Correlate requests across
+connections, HTTP/2 streams and time. Record whether a body, Authorization or Cookie
+was forwarded, never its value. A TLS/SNI change alone is not proof of a redirect.
+Include HTTP/HTTPS downgrade, cross-origin and same-origin cases where observable.
+
+For an accessible HLS master, enumerate URI lines and URI attributes in
+`EXT-X-MEDIA`, `EXT-X-I-FRAME-STREAM-INF`, `EXT-X-KEY`, `EXT-X-MAP` and related tags;
+resolve relatives against each final parent URL. Record parent → child → segment/
+key domains and every redirect. Cache hits, adaptive selection and live playlists
+mean a single watch does not exercise every listed child. Test seek/quality change.
+
+There is **no verified normal UI input** for arbitrary manifest URLs. Do not claim
+an invalid test by merely opening a URL elsewhere. If a separately authorized,
+non-pinned anonymous player response can be intercepted, a fixture proxy may replace
+only its `streamingData.hlsManifestUrl` with an HTTP, malformed-host, credential,
+bad-port or empty fixture; use reserved `.invalid`/documentation addresses and no
+real credentials. This modifies test traffic, not source, but has **not been done**.
+Keep this separate from the natural-traffic baseline; limit any expanded TLS
+inspection to the exact test origin and use no personal account. Never bypass
+pinning if it prevents the case. Require evidence that mode 2/path was exercised;
+playback success alone is insufficient. If this cannot be established within the
+unchanged release, leave N10 NOT TESTED; existing Foundation fixtures remain the
+only executed invalid-URL/fallback evidence.
+
+If decrypting actual native HLS is impossible, record parent/child/redirect and
+credential behavior as **unknown**. Browser/curl tests of a copied manifest URL
+exercise those clients, not the signed iPhone app. After testing, disable the proxy,
+remove the test CA profile/full trust, stop the proxy/RVI and restore recorded
+settings. Keep raw captures private; export only sanitized observations using the
+[empty template](Evidence/NETWORK_OBSERVATIONS_TEMPLATE.csv).
