+## 7. iPhone security checklist — all device checks NOT TESTED
+
+- **Permissions:** review Settings → Privacy & Security and the app's settings;
+  record allowed/denied states and repeat relevant features with denial. Both hosts
+  declare camera, microphone, when-in-use location, contacts, photo library, Apple
+  Music, Bluetooth, local network and tracking usage descriptions. A declaration
+  is not evidence permission was granted or data accessed. Test notification and
+  clipboard prompts where applicable; a clipboard capability is not a blanket
+  entitlement to read every other app's data.
+- **Privacy:** inspect App Privacy Report, if available/enabled, for app-attributed
+  sensor/network activity. Treat it as supporting metadata, not payload/redirect
+  evidence. Record ATT choice and background/cellular settings without claiming
+  tracker behavior from a settings switch alone.
+- **Files/cache:** inspect visible app Files locations without exporting personal
+  media. In an authorized accessible container, check Documents/Application Support/
+  Caches `YTKACE` roots for old `sabr-seed.plist` and `player-request.pb`, and temp
+  `ytkace-outgoing.pb` after launch/logout. Ordinary Files UI does not expose the
+  entire sandbox; inaccessible paths are NOT VERIFIED, not proven empty.
+- **Logout/expiry:** run N11; confirm signed-out UI, preserved legitimate media and
+  settings, no stale request reuse. Lazy expiry needs a getter/feature access after
+  inactivity. Native Google credentials, server revocation, backup copies and all
+  account-transition variants are outside fixture coverage.
+- **Diagnostics:** default logging off; briefly enable only for a controlled case,
+  inspect privately for synthetic marker leakage and URL/account/token-shaped text,
+  then disable/clear the log. Never include an actual secret in shared evidence.
+- **Background:** test audio allowed/denied, screen lock, idle and force quit;
+  distinguish active downloads/audio from optional API refresh and unrelated OS
+  traffic. Declared background modes are audio, fetch, external-accessory and
+  remote-notification; declaration is not actual scheduling evidence.
+- **Accounts/restart:** A → B → A, sign-out and cold restart; verify channel/account
+  identity locally, reauthentication and no inherited stale download authorization.
+  No jailbreak/container extraction, Keychain dump or private credential export is
+  required by this plan. Record inaccessible internals as unknown.
+- **Keychain/signing:** there is no ordinary per-app Keychain permission toggle to
+  use as an access test. Review the actual signed keychain-access groups locally
+  when tooling permits; session persistence alone does not identify which tokens
+  exist or prove their deletion. Do not export stored credentials.
+
+## 8. Attribution and evidence rules
+
+Compare identical cases with integrations off, then one on, with baseline idle and
+time markers. Distinct SponsorBlock/DeArrow/AiSList route families plus inspected
+call sites support attribution. Google domains are shared: MarufYT's player/browse,
+oEmbed and thumbnail requests can use the same hosts as native YouTube. Master-off
+still loads the tweak and does not isolate every helper. HTTP2/QUIC multiplexing,
+caches, prefetch and system traffic limit timing-only conclusions.
+
+Classify each observation as **native-likely**, **MarufYT-source-matched**,
+**system/other**, or **unresolved**, with confidence and evidence. Escalate an
+unexpected destination for source/response-chain review before labeling it
+malicious. Raw host strings and optional requests are not proof of exfiltration.
+Redact identifying hostname labels as well as URL/query/header values before any
+observation is shared. Keep raw PCAPs and decrypted data outside the repository.
+
+## 9. Final release status and limitations
+
+The two existing unsigned U01-HLS IPAs remain unchanged and are ready for the user's
+signing/device acceptance process. **They are not runtime-verified releases.** U-01
+cache/handoff remediation is supported by source order, native Foundation fixtures,
+matching compiled artifacts and independent per-IPA structure/integrity checks.
+F-01–F-04 remain intact within their tested source/fixture scope. No new confirmed
+vulnerability was established by these checks; this is not proof none exists.
+
+U-02 carrier HTTP policy, U-03 integration/privacy observations and U-04 opaque/
+dynamic destination limitations remain. Physical playback, Google login/switching,
+logout coverage, permissions, effective entitlements, background behavior, native
+HLS child/redirect security, real header forwarding and actual telemetry remain
+**NOT TESTED or unresolved**. There are no device capture results to report.
+
+No application source or version changes, rebuilds, merges, pushes or protected
+branch modifications were performed during this final verification. Only the new
+`Documentation/FINAL_VERIFICATION/` report/evidence was written.
